nodecode-citation-guard is a rewrite of ChienNguyen23's ChienNguyen23/hermes-citation-guard:

  https://github.com/ChienNguyen23/hermes-citation-guard
  commit 6916b2ae7f561765883c57b32441db049e246113
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Chien Nguyen (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract. The checks are the
same against the same four registries (doi.org, Crossref, PubMed, arXiv),
the verdicts are the same, and the two surfaces are the same -- the
verify_citations tool and the /citecheck command -- now one NLE:DEFINE-CELL
declaration with its stop derived from it. Ported from __init__.py,
extract.py, sources.py, verify.py and render.py: reference-list and BibTeX
parsing, DOI/PMID/arXiv extraction, identifier resolution, the title, year
and first-author comparison, retraction and expression-of-concern lookup
through Crossref's update notices and PubMed's publication types, and the
report text.

Left out, and why: the transform_llm_output reply guard, which appended a
warning footer to every reply that cited a bad reference -- Nodecode's hook
points are the tool dispatch and the live frame, so this cell tells the
model to check a bibliography before presenting it instead, in the manual
line every request carries; the 7-day registry cache on disk, of which this
cell keeps an in-memory one per start; and the original's per-host rate
gates and 10-minute backoff. Manuscripts in .docx are read through unzip
rather than Python's zipfile. DataCite and the other DOI agencies are still
asked when Crossref does not know an id. The optional contact address and
NCBI key are still sent, to Crossref and NCBI and to nothing else.
